  "tagline": "Academic native XML DBMS from ISP RAS with full ACID transactions; long since abandoned.",
  "description": "Sedna was a native XML database developed at the Institute for System Programming of the Russian Academy of Sciences. It was notable for full ACID transactions, an XQuery implementation with XUpdate-style updates, triggers, full-text indexing and a custom memory-mapped storage layer designed for large XML documents. It had a real following in the late 2000s as a free, transactional alternative to commercial XML stores. Development stopped around 2011, the public GitHub mirror has not changed since 2017 and the project site is offline, so new XML work should use BaseX or eXist-db.",
